#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grover's algorithm description"
msgstr "Paglalarawan ng algorithm ni Grover"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description of Grover's algorithm {#description-of-grovers-algorithm}"
msgstr "Paglalarawan ng algorithm ni Grover {#description-of-grovers-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we'll describe Grover's algorithm.\n"
"We'll begin by discussing *phase query gates* and how to build them, followed by the description of Grover's algorithm itself.\n"
"Finally, we'll briefly discuss how this algorithm is naturally applied to searching.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa seksyong ito, ilalarawan natin ang algorithm ni Grover.\n"
"Magsisimula tayo sa pagtalakay sa *phase query gates* at kung paano itayo ang mga ito, kasunod ng paglalarawan ng algorithm mismo.\n"
"Sa huli, tatalakayin natin nang maikli kung paano natural na inilalapat ang algorithm na ito sa paghahanap.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase query gates {#phase-query-gates}"
msgstr "Mga phase query gate {#phase-query-gates}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grover's algorithm makes use of operations known as *phase query gates*.\n"
"In contrast to an ordinary query gate $U_f$, defined for a given function $f$ in the usual way described previously, a phase query gate for the function $f$ is defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang algorithm ni Grover ng mga operasyong kilala bilang *phase query gates*.\n"
"Kaiba sa isang ordinaryong query gate na $U_f$, na tinukoy para sa isang ibinigay na function na $f$ sa karaniwang paraan na inilarawan dati, ang phase query gate para sa function na $f$ ay tinukoy bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert x\\rangle = (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert x\\rangle = (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "para sa bawat string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operation $Z_f$ can be implemented using one query gate $U_f$ as this diagram suggests:\n"
msgstr "Ang operasyong $Z_f$ ay maaaring ipatupad gamit ang isang query gate na $U_f$ gaya ng iminumungkahi ng diagram na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit implementing a Z_f gate using one query gate together with the phase kickback phenomenon](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Z_f.svg)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit implementing a Z_f gate using one query gate together with the phase kickback phenomenon](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Z_f.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implementation makes use of the phase kickback phenomenon, and requires that one workspace qubit, initialized to a $\\vert -\\rangle$ state, is made available.\n"
"This qubit remains in the $\\vert - \\rangle$ state after the implementation has completed, and can be reused (to implement subsequent $Z_f$ gates, for instance) or simply discarded.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang implementasyong ito ng phenomenon na phase kickback, at kailangan nitong magkaroon ng isang workspace qubit, na sinimulan sa $\\vert -\\rangle$ na estado.\n"
"Nananatili ang qubit na ito sa $\\vert - \\rangle$ na estado pagkatapos makumpleto ang implementasyon, at maaaring gamitin ulit (para ipatupad ang mga kasunod na $Z_f$ gate, halimbawa) o basta itapon na lang.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the operation $Z_f$, we will also make use of a phase query gate for the $n$-bit OR function, which is defined as follows for each string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa operasyong $Z_f$, gagamitin din natin ang isang phase query gate para sa $n$-bit OR function, na tinukoy tulad ng sumusunod para sa bawat string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{OR}(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  0 & x = 0^n\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"  1 & x \\neq 0^n\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{OR}(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  0 & x = 0^n\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"  1 & x \\neq 0^n\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explicitly, the phase query gate for the $n$-bit OR function operates like this:\n"
msgstr "Partikular, ang phase query gate para sa $n$-bit OR function ay gumagana nang ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"- \\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n.\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"- \\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n.\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To be clear, this is how $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ operates on standard basis states; its behavior on arbitrary states is determined from this expression by linearity.\n"
msgstr "Para maging malinaw, ito ang paraan ng paggana ng $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ sa mga standard basis state; ang gawi nito sa mga arbitrary na estado ay natutukoy mula sa expression na ito sa pamamagitan ng linearity.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ can be implemented as a quantum circuit by beginning with a Boolean circuit for the OR function, then constructing a $U_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ operation (that is, a standard query gate for the $n$-bit OR function) using the procedure described in the *Quantum algorithmic foundations* lesson, and finally a $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ operation using the phase kickback phenomenon as described above.\n"
"Notice that the operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ has no dependence on the function $f$ and can therefore be implemented by a quantum circuit having no query gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyong $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ ay maaaring ipatupad bilang isang quantum circuit sa pamamagitan ng pagsisimula sa isang Boolean circuit para sa OR function, pagkatapos ay gumawa ng operasyong $U_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ (iyon ay, isang standard query gate para sa $n$-bit OR function) gamit ang pamamaraang inilarawan sa aralin na *Quantum algorithmic foundations*, at sa wakas ang operasyong $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ gamit ang phase kickback phenomenon gaya ng inilarawan sa itaas.\n"
"Pansinin na ang operasyong $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ ay walang dependensya (pag-asa) sa function na $f$ kaya maaari itong ipatupad ng isang quantum circuit na walang mga query gate.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description of the algorithm {#description-of-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Paglalarawan ng algorithm {#description-of-the-algorithm}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have the two operations $Z_f$ and $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$, we can describe Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Ngayong mayroon na tayong dalawang operasyong $Z_f$ at $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$, maaari na nating ilarawan ang algorithm ni Grover.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The algorithm refers to a number $t$, which is the number of *iterations* it performs (and therefore the number of *queries* to the function $f$ it requires).\n"
"This number $t$ isn't specified by Grover's algorithm as we're describing it, and we'll discuss later in the lesson how it can be chosen.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binabanggit ng algorithm ang isang bilang na $t$, na siyang bilang ng mga *iteration* na ginagawa nito (at samakatuwid ang bilang ng mga *query* sa function na $f$ na kailangan nito).\n"
"Hindi tinutukoy ng algorithm ni Grover ang bilang na $t$ na ito ayon sa ating paglalarawan, at tatalakayin natin sa ibang pagkakataon sa aralin kung paano ito pipiliin.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Grover's algorithm\">\n"
"1. Initialize an $n$ qubit register $\\mathsf{Q}$ to the all-zero state $\\vert 0^n \\rangle$ and then apply a Hadamard operation to each qubit of $\\mathsf{Q}$.\n"
"2. Apply $t$ times the unitary operation $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ to the register $\\mathsf{Q}$\n"
"3. Measure the qubits of $\\mathsf{Q}$ with respect to standard basis measurements and output the resulting string.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Algorithm ni Grover\">\n"
"1. I-initialize ang isang $n$ qubit register na $\\mathsf{Q}$ sa all-zero state na $\\vert 0^n \\rangle$ at pagkatapos ay mag-apply ng Hadamard operation sa bawat qubit ng $\\mathsf{Q}$.\n"
"2. I-apply nang $t$ beses ang unitary operation na $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ sa register na $\\mathsf{Q}$\n"
"3. Sukatin ang mga qubit ng $\\mathsf{Q}$ gamit ang mga standard basis measurement at i-output ang resultang string.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ iterated in step 2 will be called the *Grover operation* throughout the remainder of this lesson.\n"
"Here is a quantum circuit representation of the Grover operation when $n=7\\!:$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyong $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ na paulit-ulit sa hakbang 2 ay tatawagin na *Grover operation* sa natitirang bahagi ng araling ito.\n"
"Narito ang isang quantum circuit na representasyon ng Grover operation kapag $n=7\\!:$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit representation of the Grover operation](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_operation.svg)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit representation of the Grover operation](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_operation.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram, the $Z_f$ operation is depicted as being larger than $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ as an informal visual clue to suggest that it is likely to be the more costly operation.\n"
"In particular, when we're working within the query model, $Z_f$ requires one query while $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ requires no queries.\n"
"If instead we have a Boolean circuit for the function $f$, and then convert it to a quantum circuit for $Z_f$, we can reasonably expect that the resulting quantum circuit will be larger and more complicated than one for $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa diagram na ito, ang operasyong $Z_f$ ay inilalarawan na mas malaki kaysa sa $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ bilang isang impormal na biswal na pahiwatig na malamang na ito ang mas mahal na operasyon.\n"
"Partikular, kapag nagtatrabaho tayo sa loob ng query model, ang $Z_f$ ay nangangailangan ng isang query habang ang $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ ay hindi nangangailangan ng mga query.\n"
"Kung sa halip mayroon tayong Boolean circuit para sa function na $f,$ at pagkatapos ay i-convert ito sa isang quantum circuit para sa $Z_f,$ maaari tayong makatwirang asahan na ang resultang quantum circuit ay magiging mas malaki at mas kumplikado kaysa sa isang para sa $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a diagram of a quantum circuit for the entire algorithm when $n=7$ and $t=3$.\n"
"For larger values of $t$ we can simply insert additional instances of the Grover operation immediately before the measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang isang diagram ng isang quantum circuit para sa buong algorithm kapag $n=7$ at $t=3$.\n"
"Para sa mas malalaking halaga ng $t$ maaari tayong magsingit ng mga karagdagang instance ng Grover operation agad bago ang mga sukat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit for Grover's algorithm when t=3](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit for Grover's algorithm when t=3](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Application to search {#application-to-search}"
msgstr "Paglalapat sa paghahanap {#application-to-search}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grover's algorithm can be applied to the *Search* problem as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang algorithm ni Grover ay maaaring ilapat sa problemang *Search* tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the number $t$ in step 2. (This is discussed later in the lesson.)\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng bilang na $t$ sa hakbang 2. (Ito ay tatalakayin sa ibang pagkakataon sa aralin.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run Grover's algorithm on the function $f$, using whatever choice we made for $t$, to obtain a string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang algorithm ni Grover sa function na $f$, gamit ang anumang pagpili na ginawa natin para sa $t$, para makakuha ng string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query the function $f$ on the string $x$ to see if it's a valid solution:\n"
msgstr "I-query ang function na $f$ sa string na $x$ para malaman kung ito ay valid na solusyon:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $f(x) = 1$, then we have found a solution, so we can stop and output $x$.\n"
msgstr "Kung $f(x) = 1$, nakahanap na tayo ng solusyon, kaya maaari tayong huminto at i-output ang $x$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Otherwise, if $f(x) = 0$, then we can either run the procedure again, possibly with a different choice for $t$, or we can decide to give up and output \"no solution.\"\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi, kung $f(x) = 0$, maaari tayong muling patakbuhin ang pamamaraan, posibleng may ibang pagpili para sa $t$, o maaari tayong magpasyang sumuko at i-output ang \"walang solusyon.\"\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we've analyzed how Grover's algorithm works, we'll see that by taking $t = O(\\sqrt{N})$, we obtain a solution to our search problem (if one exists) with high probability.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nasuri na natin kung paano gumagana ang algorithm ni Grover, makikita natin na sa pag-take ng $t = O(\\sqrt{N})$, makakakuha tayo ng solusyon sa ating search problem (kung mayroon) nang may mataas na posibilidad.\n"
